schema: "0.4"
id: fim-notebook-livebook-and-widgets-kino-plotly-04-edge-integration-state-accessibility
type: visualization
quality: high
solution: kino-plotly
category: notebook-livebook-and-widgets
variant: edge-integration-state-accessibility
prompt:
  system: |-
    You are a senior Elixir Livebook scientific visualization engineer. Output only one complete ASCII Elixir Livebook code cell for Kino.Plotly with an optional Kino.JS fallback. No Markdown fences, no prose outside code. Prioritize validation, wrapper fallback, accessibility, and safe execution.
  text: |-
    Create a Kino.Plotly edge/integration cell that validates incoming numeric records or matrices, rejects malformed shapes, builds a safe Plotly trace list and layout, and renders with Kino.Plotly.new/2. If Kino.Plotly is unavailable, include a guarded Kino.JS fallback module that imports a pinned Plotly.js script with ctx.importJS and calls Plotly.newPlot on a local div with responsive config.

    Requirements: document Livebook compatibility, trace data shape, z matrix orientation, wrapper availability, and browser limits; include fallback local data, validation diagnostics, accessible labels, hover text, and color scale legends; include safe execution checks for remote asset failure, huge traces, credentials, eval, shell calls, untrusted JSON, and non-serializable data.
  provider_options:
    max_tokens: 8192
    temperature: 0.2
    top_p: 0.9
output:
  text_format: elixir
  artifact_kind: livebook-kino-plotly-edge-cell
  formats:
  - format: exs
evaluation:
  checklist:
  - "Import check: generated code installs kino_plotly and kino, uses Kino.Plotly.new/2 primarily, and optionally defines a guarded Kino.JS fallback."
  - "Notebook compatibility: comments identify Livebook/Kino, Plotly.js browser rendering, and wrapper availability."
  - "Reactive state: validated data drives figure rebuilds or fallback rendering without unbounded browser loops."
  - "Data shape: numeric records, arrays, z matrices, rejected rows, trace maps, and layout maps are documented."
  - "Accessibility and fallback: diagnostics, fallback data, axis labels, hover text, color legends, and fallback renderer status are present."
  - "Safe execution: no huge traces, credentials, eval, shell commands, untrusted JSON execution, or unguarded remote asset assumptions."
  rubric:
  - name: Format validity
    weight: 30
    criteria:
    - "Output is one complete ASCII Elixir Livebook code cell with no Markdown fences or explanatory wrapper."
    - "The code is valid and separates validation, figure construction, primary render, and fallback render."
    - "The optional Kino.JS fallback uses current module asset syntax and init(ctx, data)."
  - name: Semantic completeness
    weight: 30
    criteria:
    - "Implements shape validation, diagnostics, Plotly rendering, local fallback data, and guarded wrapper fallback."
    - "Uses Plotly-specific trace and layout semantics correctly for the selected chart type."
    - "Includes notebook/livebook compatibility, reactive state, data shape, accessibility, fallback, and safe execution checks."
  - name: UX/structural quality
    weight: 25
    criteria:
    - "Users can see why data was accepted or rejected before viewing the chart."
    - "Charts include accessible labels, hover text, and readable color scales."
    - "Fallback renderer status is explicit and non-disruptive."
  - name: Robustness
    weight: 15
    criteria:
    - "Handles empty data, malformed matrices, mismatched lengths, extreme values, wrapper absence, and asset load failure."
    - "Keeps all primary data local, deterministic, and bounded."
    - "Documents performance and security boundaries for browser-rendered figures."
  pass_conditions:
  - "All required YAML fields are present and the generated artifact is one valid ASCII Elixir Livebook cell."
  - "Rubric weights are exactly Format validity 30, Semantic completeness 30, UX/structural quality 25, Robustness 15."
  - "The prompt requires notebook/livebook compatibility, reactive state, data shape, accessibility, fallback, and safe execution checks."
  - "The solution remains Kino.Plotly-centered while providing a guarded Kino.JS fallback for wrapper gaps."
tags:
- fim
- notebook-livebook-and-widgets
- livebook
- kino-plotly
- edge-integration-state-accessibility
